From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: read living-seat LP without changing Lua scope

The LP comparison overlay must inspect every living opponent even in a
bound effect or nested MPNthDuelist rebind. Give it a read-only real-seat
query rather than temporarily replacing the caller's scope. Stock GetLP
and every 1v1/Tag card script keep their existing behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/libduel.cpp b/libduel.cpp
--- a/libduel.cpp
+++ b/libduel.cpp
@@ -5366,2 +5366,15 @@
 }
+// Read one living real seat's LP without changing the Lua perspective or opponent binding.
+// Used by the multiplayer LP comparison overlay, including inside an existing seat rebind.
+LUA_STATIC_FUNCTION(MPGetLP) {
+	check_param_count(L, 1);
+	const auto seat = lua_get<int64_t>(L, 1);
+	const auto& f = *pduel->game_field;
+	if(seat < 0 || seat >= f.n_duelists || !f.is_alive(static_cast<uint8_t>(seat))) {
+		lua_pushnil(L);
+		return 1;
+	}
+	lua_pushinteger(L, pduel->game_field->lp_ref(static_cast<uint8_t>(seat)));
+	return 1;
+}
 // Duel.MPAttackedSeat(): the real seat of the duelist that the current attack goes at (the controller of the attack target, or the
